WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.320
Steam curls up from a pan.

2
00:00:02.370 --> 00:00:04.840
Without looking, you grab the handle.

3
00:00:04.890 --> 00:00:06.830
Your hand snaps away.

4
00:00:06.880 --> 00:00:10.020
Only then do you feel it and shout ow.

5
00:00:10.070 --> 00:00:11.840
You never chose to move.

6
00:00:11.890 --> 00:00:14.140
So what moved your hand?

7
00:00:14.190 --> 00:00:18.350
In this mission, you'll meet the two
main divisions of your nervous system:

8
00:00:18.400 --> 00:00:22.100
your central nervous system, which
is the brain and the spinal cord,

9
00:00:22.150 --> 00:00:24.370
and your peripheral nervous system.

10
00:00:24.420 --> 00:00:28.420
Peripheral nerves link your brain and
spinal cord to the rest of your body,

11
00:00:28.470 --> 00:00:30.730
carrying messages both ways.

12
00:00:30.780 --> 00:00:34.340
And you'll see what your central
nervous system does with a message:

13
00:00:34.390 --> 00:00:39.430
receive it, process it, and send
instructions to muscles and glands.

14
00:00:39.480 --> 00:00:43.890
Your mission: work out what moved
your hand before you decided to.
